Implement user story SKY-002-test-tc1: Write vitest tests for SkyscannerClient with mocked fetch (part 1/2)

## Story Description
Create src/skyscanner/client.test.ts with vitest tests that mock global fetch (no real network calls). Covers URL/header construction, successful parsing, HTTP errors, missing key, malformed responses, and mock-mode behavior.

## Acceptance Criteria
- client.test.ts uses vitest with mocked fetch (vi.stubGlobal or equivalent) and afterEach restoration; no real network calls are made
- Test verifies correct RapidAPI URL and header construction (including X-RapidAPI-Key header)
- Test verifies successful API response is parsed into FlightResult[] matching the interface
- Test verifies HTTP 4xx/5xx responses cause searchFlights to reject with an Error containing the status code
- Test verifies missing or empty apiKey (constructor arg and RAPIDAPI_KEY env) throws the missing-key Error
- Test verifies malformed/missing-fields response body causes searchFlights to reject with a parse/validation Error
- Test verifies MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API='true' returns fixture data without invoking fetch; non-'true' values perform real fetch
- tsc --noEmit exits 0 and vitest run exits 0 with all tests passing


## Test Criteria (ground truth — written from actual source; overrides any conflicting AC)
- Class SkyscannerClient is exported from module
- Constructor signature: constructor({ apiKey }: { apiKey?: string } = {})
- Constructor throws Error with exact message: 'SkyscannerClient: missing API key. Provide apiKey in the constructor or set the RAPIDAPI_KEY environment variable.' when apiKey is undefined/null/empty and RAPIDAPI_KEY env var is also missing/empty
- Constructor resolves apiKey from constructor argument first, then falls back to process.env.RAPIDAPI_KEY
- Method signature: async searchFlights(params: SearchParams): Promise<FlightResult[]>
- SearchParams interface: { origin: string; destination: string; date: string; adults?: number }
- FlightResult interface: { price: number; currency: string; airline: string; departure: string; arrival: string; duration: number; stops: number }
- When process.env.MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API === 'true' (exact string match), searchFlights returns fixture data from getMockFixture without calling fetch
- When MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API is any value other than 'true' (including 'TRUE', '1', 'yes', undefined), searchFlights performs real fetch call
- RapidAPI endpoint URL: https://skyscanner44.p.rapidapi.com/search
- Query param 'from' is set from params.origin
- Query param 'to' is set from params.destination
- Query param 'depart_date' is set from params.date
- Query param 'adults' is set only when params.adults !== undefined
- Request headers include: 'X-RapidAPI-Key': this.#apiKey and 'X-RapidAPI-Host': 'skyscanner44.p.rapidapi.com'
- Network errors throw Error with message starting with 'SkyscannerClient: network error during flight search:'
- HTTP 4xx/5xx responses throw Error with exact message pattern: 'SkyscannerClient: flight search failed with HTTP status ${response.status}'
- Invalid JSON response throws Error with message starting with 'SkyscannerClient: failed to parse response JSON:'
- Non-array response body throws Error: 'SkyscannerClient: expected response body to be an array of flight results'
- Each array item is validated - null/non-object items throw Error: 'SkyscannerClient: flight result at index ${i} is not an object'
- Missing required fields throw Error: 'SkyscannerClient: flight result at index ${i} is missing required field "${field}"'
- Invalid price throws Error: 'SkyscannerClient: flight result at index ${i} has an invalid "price" (expected finite number)'
- Invalid currency throws Error: 'SkyscannerClient: flight result at index ${i} has an invalid "currency" (expected non-empty string)'
- Invalid airline throws Error: 'SkyscannerClient: flight result at index ${i} has an invalid "airline" (expected non-empty string)'
- Invalid departure throws Error: 'SkyscannerClient: flight result at index ${i} has an invalid "departure" (expected non-empty string)'
- Invalid arrival throws Error: 'SkyscannerClient: flight result at index ${i} has an invalid "arrival" (expected non-empty string)'
- Invalid duration throws Error: 'SkyscannerClient: flight result at index ${i} has an invalid "duration" (expected finite number)'
- Invalid stops throws Error: 'SkyscannerClient: flight result at index ${i} has an invalid "stops" (expected non-negative integer)'
- Mock fixture returns exactly 3 FlightResult objects with varying prices (149, 199, 329), all with currency 'USD'
- No validation exists for adults being positive - adults=0 is accepted

## Mock Strategy
```typescript
vi.mock('<import-path-to-SkyscannerClient>', () => ({
  SkyscannerClient: vi.fn().mockImplementation(() => ({
    searchFlights: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(undefined),
  })),
}));
```

